# ⚠ THE LEADING BACKSLASH ON '\!Revisions' IS REQUIRED.
#
# '!' starts a NEGATION pattern in gitignore. The release folder is literally
# named '!Revisions', so an unescaped '!Revisions/*.zip' is parsed as
# "un-ignore Revisions/*.zip" -- a silent no-op. That mistake shipped on
# 2026-10-01 and pushed 25 release zips (14.34 MiB) to the remote. Verified
# with `git check-ignore -v` after escaping.

# --- Python bytecode (48 .pyc files were tracked until 2026-10-01) ---
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*.pyo

# --- Credentials and runtime config ---
# autotester_config.txt holds NETBOX_TOKEN in plaintext (NETBOX_TOKEN is NOT
# migrated to the OS credential store). Only the .example belongs in the repo.
autotester_config.txt
.secure_fallback.json
*.pem
*.key

# --- Per-run state and reports: machine-local, not source ---
ospf_stability_state.json
*.xlsx
autotester_*.txt
gsx_perfmon_*.txt
site_sweep_*.txt
health_check_*.txt
interface_check_*.txt
ds1_pms_*.txt
*_connect_fail.txt

# --- Release artifacts: build output, not source ---
# The canonical CHANGELOG lives at '!Revisions/CHANGELOG.md' and IS tracked
# (negated at the bottom of this file). Everything else under there is built.
\!Revisions/*.zip
\!Revisions/Production/
\!Revisions/Curveball*/
# Orphaned temp files from interrupted zip writes (random 8-char names).
\!Revisions/zi??????

# --- Windows launcher cruft ---
*.lnk
# Artifact of a path-handling bug: a literal 'C:\Claude' directory created
# inside the project.
C:\\Claude/

# --- Internal working notes, not for the shared repo ---
SYSTEMS_MEETING_PREP.md

# --- Re-include things the blanket rules above would wrongly catch ---
# 'autotester_*.txt' is meant for run reports, but it also matches the example
# config template, which DOES belong in the repo. Caught by a check-ignore
# test, not by reading the file.
!autotester_config.example.txt
!\!Revisions/CHANGELOG.md
